From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: allow SD supply load votes

SDHCI requests active loads for the external card's L18 and L21 supplies,
but the inherited regulator constraints do not allow those votes to reach
RPM. The SM-T531 vendor configuration explicitly switches both supplies
between low and high load, with active requests of 800 mA and 22 mA.

Allow the existing upstream regulator and SDHCI drivers to propagate their
load requests. Do not change voltages or add a board-specific driver.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -109,3 +109,11 @@
 	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	no-1-8-v;
 };
+
+&pm8226_l18 {
+	regulator-allow-set-load;
+};
+
+&pm8226_l21 {
+	regulator-allow-set-load;
+};
-- 
2.53.0
